{
  "dom_id": "step-q69236",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{{6}^{4}}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[3]{{6}^{4}},$ we get $x={6}^{4}$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{{6}^{4}}={({6}^{4})}^{1/3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the power law for exponents, we have\n\n$$\n{({6}^{4})}^{1/3}={6}^{4/3}.\n$$",
